WEBVTT

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:11.900
<v Michael>The lantern market at Thornwick is closing for the night. Stalls are folding their awnings.

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:17.100
<v Michael>An old woman with a cart of brass lanterns waves you over.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:22.800
<v Michael>Lantern for the road? The bridge watch won't let you pass without one after dark.

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:27.000
<v Jo>How much for one?

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:31.600
<v Michael>Three copper. And a word of advice: don't buy the green ones.

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:35.400
<v Sam>Why not the green ones?

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:42.700
<v Michael>She lowers her voice. Green light is what the toll-keeper's men look for. They take whoever carries it.

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:48.100
<v Jo>I bet the toll-keeper is the one selling the green lanterns in the first place.

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:53.900
<v Sam>We buy two plain ones and head for the bridge before the bell.

00:00:54.400 --> 00:01:02.200
<v Michael>The bell rings ten. The bridge closes at midnight, so you have two hours.

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:04.100
<v Michael>What do you do?
